From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 18:53:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] perf(dsv41): dedicated R=3 decode dense
 indexer_score_v41 with wave-aligned CTAs


Add a dedicated R=3 multi-row KPool-reusing dense indexer_score_v41 kernel
for decode (rows <= 96) with wave-aligned CTA caps (144 <=256K, 288 >256K)
and loaded_page fallback dedup, setting _BLOCKMAX_MIN_ROWS = 97 so wide
prefill (rows >= 97) cleanly stays on BlockMax-32.

Upstream-base: 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354
Rationale: Cut Cold-DRAM dense decode indexer latency -17.1% at 8x6 @256K
           (-1.31 ms/8L), -27.4% at 8x6 @1M (-9.39 ms/8L), and -24.2% at
           16x6 @1M (-16.15 ms/8L) with zero short-context regression.
Quality: uint16 bit-exact scores/top-k; 128/128 live greedy match.
Tests: 107/107 indexer + tilelang + PDL tests + 2-boot live tp3 screen
       (fl25 = -0.009%, PR #1276).
Upstream-status: Local DeepSeek-V4.1 TileLang decode indexer optimization.
